# zig-only
# The statusline carries a clock beside the bell: its menu offers Local
# / UTC / Hide, and clock.utc / hide / local switch it. (The menu is
# opened first: the switches' toasts stack over the corner it anchors
# in.) The UTC chip reads `HH:MMZ ` — the Z, its pad, then the
# workspace chip's arrow.
write a.txt alpha
open a.txt
command clock.menu
expect screen contains "╭ Clock"
expect screen contains "Local time"
expect screen contains "Hide the clock"
key esc
expect screen lacks "╭ Clock"
command clock.utc
expect screen contains "clock: UTC"
expect screen contains "Z "
command clock.hide
expect screen contains "clock: hidden"
expect screen lacks "Z "
command clock.local
expect screen contains "clock: local time"
